0(\u0001\u0000\u0000\u001e\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�o\u0000\u0000customXml/_rels/item1.xml.relsPK\u0005\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0012\u0000�\u0004\u0000\u0000�q\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000","minutes_text":"LA VERNE YOUTH & FAMILY ACTION COMMITTEE\n  Minutes of the Regular Meeting\n  December 10, 2024\n\n1. A meeting of the Youth & Family Action Committee was called to order by Council\n  Member Rick Crosby at 5:01 p.m.\n\n  Executive Board Members present:\n\n  Executive Board\n  Rick Crosby, Council Member\n  Don Kendrick, Resident\n  Denise Fisher, Resident\n\n2. Review of Minutes  Minutes for the October 29, 2024, meeting were\n  approved with Council Member Lau and BUSD Board\n  Member Palatto absent.\n\n3. SRO Report  School Resource Officer Burgos provided an update\n  on the upcoming softball game scheduled for\n  December 12 at 5:00 PM, featuring participants from\n  the district, LVPD, LVFD, and Bonita High School. The\n  event will serve as a fundraiser for the Spark of Love\n  campaign. Additionally, SRO Burgos reported on a\n  recent meeting with local School Resource Officers\n  (SROs) from multiple agencies, where they discussed\n  various strategies to support students. The group\n  plans to hold quarterly meetings to continue sharing\n  ideas and best practices.\n\n4. CRR Specialist Report  Community Risk Reduction Specialist Lonnie\n  provided an update on the Explorers program,\n  highlighting the participants' learning experiences in\n  the fire service as well as their ongoing community\n  outreach efforts. CRRS Shipman also introduced\n  Jennifer Brown, Senior Management Analyst, to\n  discuss the department’s involvement with the Spark\n  of Love program. Ms. Brown explained that the\n  program aims to expand partnerships with local non-\n  profits and school districts, including counselors, to\n  better identify and support families in the coming\n  years. She noted that 50 students at Leroy Haynes\n  currently benefit from the program. Additionally,\n  Denise shared her 13-year commitment to assisting\n  families in the school district, mentioning that her\n  group is fulfilling wish lists for 150 students this year.\n  The group also discussed potential future\n\fYouth & Family Action Committee Minutes December 10, 2024, page 2\n\n  collaborations between Denise’s initiative and the\n  Spark of Love program.\n\n5. BUSD Report  BUSD Representative Steven Patterson shared via\n  emailed notes on November 21, nine students from\n  Bonita and San Dimas High Schools earned welding\n  certifications through a 16-week Career Technical\n  Education (CTE) pilot program in partnership with\n  Pomona Valley America’s Job Center of California\n  (AJCC) and the Los Angeles County Department of\n  Economic Opportunity (LACDEO). Organized by CTE\n  Coordinator Vanessa Tilford, the program provided\n  tuition-free training at the Welding Certification Center\n  (WCC), preparing students for well-paying welding\n  careers. Additionally, under the leadership of Dr. Kim\n  Lawe, Bonita Unified has enhanced support for\n  English Language Learners (ELL) in grades K-12.\n  Through designated and integrated strategies,\n  administrators and staff aim to accelerate fluency and\n  improve student outcomes.\n\n6. BUSD Student Update  Lauren shared with the committee that the choir show\n  is coming up the following weekend at the Bonita\n  Center for the Arts. There has been a lot going on with\n  sports which has been exciting for students. She also\n  shared that the Chamber Singers performed at\n  Candlelight at Disneyland. There is also going to be a\n  kids cheer clinic at Bonita High School in January.\n\n7. Utility Box Art Project  YFAC Chair Rick Crosby shared an update regarding\n  this project on behalf of Assistant City Manager JR\n  Ranells. He shared that the committee has not yet\n  heard back from ULV regarding their potential interest\n  in the project. The City is reaching out to other\n  community members who have done art around the\n  city, who might be able to serve as mentors.\n\n8. Parent Education Night  YFAC Chair Council Member Crosby shared with the\n  Committee that we are currently coordinating with the\n  Roynon principal to figure out a date for this event.\n  Once a date is set the next step will be to discuss the\n  agenda and the presentation. LVPD will also assist\n  with this presentation.\n\fYouth & Family Action Committee Minutes December 10, 2024, page 3\n\n9. Public Comment  YFAC Chair Crosby shared how much kindness\n  means in this season and he encouraged the group to\n  give grace this season and check in with others.\n\n10. Next Meeting  The next YFAC meeting was scheduled for January\n  28, 2025 at 5:00pm.\n\n11. Adjournment  The meeting was adjourned at 5:27 p.m.\n\nRespectfully submitted,\n\nErin Beilstein\nSenior Management Analyst"}